From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cera <cera@local>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:25:31 -0700
Subject: fix(dart): preserve declaration order for callback-trait vtable slots

Methods were sorted alphabetically for every object. For a foreign-implementable
trait the method order IS the vtable slot order and has to match the Rust
vtable, so sorting silently misaligned every slot past the first: calls landed
on the wrong method with the wrong signature.

Regular objects keep the sort, where each method has its own FFI symbol and the
order is cosmetic.
---
 src/dart/parsing.rs | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dart/parsing.rs b/src/dart/parsing.rs
index 8d439f7..a579740 100644
--- a/src/dart/parsing.rs
+++ b/src/dart/parsing.rs
@@ -411,8 +411,15 @@ pub(super) fn component_interface_to_metadata(
                     }],
                 });
             }
-            methods.sort_by(|a, b| a.name.cmp(&b.name));
-            methods.dedup_by(|a, b| a.name == b.name);
+            // For foreign-implementable traits (callback interfaces) the method
+            // order IS the vtable slot order, which must match UniFFI's Rust
+            // vtable (declaration order). Sorting alphabetically here would
+            // misalign the slots, so only sort/dedup for regular objects (where
+            // each method has its own FFI symbol and order is cosmetic).
+            if !obj.has_callback_interface() {
+                methods.sort_by(|a, b| a.name.cmp(&b.name));
+                methods.dedup_by(|a, b| a.name == b.name);
+            }
 
             UdlObject {
                 name: obj.name().to_string(),
